{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST parse Rust, Python, TypeScript, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML\nsources with pinned tree-sitter grammars, selected by file extension compared\ncase-insensitively. A source with any syntax error MUST fail to parse, reporting\nthe line of its first error. Every\nother text file MUST use a plain-text profile in which each line that is not\nblank is an anonymous outline node of kind `line`. Each supported language MUST\nhave an outline profile that maps grammar node kinds to short outline kind names\nand, for each mapped kind, states whether a node is named, and by which fields\nor children, or anonymous. Only mapped kinds MUST appear in the outline, except\nthat a Markdown profile MAY additionally recognize colon-fenced directive\ncontainers under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.fence_precedence`\nand expose them as outline nodes under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.fenced_blocks`. Such containers MUST\npreserve source ranges and containment, and MUST NOT be recognized within\nliteral code or raw HTML. Other nodes MUST be transparent, so their outline\ndescendants appear under the nearest outline ancestor. A profile MAY attach grammar siblings to an outline\nnode, such as Rust attributes and doc comments preceding an item, so the outline\ntree need not match the grammar tree exactly; attached siblings are part of that\nnode for its line range and hash. Every file's outline MUST have a root node\nfor the whole file, independent of language. Source in no other outline node,\nsuch as top-level statements no profile maps, MUST belong to the root node;\nprofiles MUST NOT invent fallback kinds for it. Comments MUST NOT be outline nodes. Profiles MUST be\ndocumented. Upgrading a grammar or profile MAY change outlines and MUST be\ntreated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check each obligation in `requirements.references.outlines`.\n\n**Language and extension selection**\n- `profiles_are_selected_by_extension_case_insensitively` checks upper- and mixed-case extensions (`.RS`, `.Py`, `.TSX`, `.MD`, `.TOML`). It also checks that a file with no extension and `notes.rs.txt` fall to `plain-text`.\n- `every_profile_mapping_is_documented` checks that every profile extension is in the reference table.\n- `grammar_dependencies_are_pinned_to_exact_versions` checks that each `habeas-language-*` crate pins its tree-sitter grammars to an exact version. This covers the \"pinned grammars\" and \"deliberate change\" obligations.\n\n**Syntax errors**\n- `reports_parse_failures_with_lines` checks Rust, Python, and TOML. For TOML, a later broken line exists after the first one. The test asserts that the first error's line is the one reported and that the message starts with the line prefix.\n- I read `check_errors` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/outline/mod.rs` to see whether error detection is language-specific. It is one generic routine over all grammars, so the lack of per-language error tests for CSS, TS, YAML, and Markdown does not leave a distinct conditional untested.\n\n**Plain-text profile**\n- `plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes` checks that only non-blank lines become nodes, that the kind is `line`, and that they are anonymous (`line@…` selectors).\n- `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` checks the same through the outline tool.\n\n**Per-language profiles and naming rules**\n- Tests cover each language:\n  - Python: `python_profile_outlines_defs_classes_and_statements`\n  - TypeScript and TSX: `typescript_profile_outlines_declarations`\n  - CSS: `css_profile_names_rules_by_normalized_selectors`\n  - Markdown: `markdown_profile_nests_sections_by_heading`\n  - TOML and YAML: `toml_and_yaml_profiles_name_keys`\n  - Rust: `rust_selectors_follow_syntactic_ancestry`, `selectors_name_syntactic_ancestry_and_duplicates`, and `item_macros_are_anonymous_nodes_and_expression_macros_are_not`\n- `markdown_views_respect_profile_field_and_child_naming_rules` covers the named-by-field, named-by-child, and anonymous cases.\n\n**Only mapped kinds appear; other nodes are transparent**\n- `profile_rules_map_only_matching_contexts_and_keep_other_nodes_transparent` shows an unmapped node's descendants attaching to the nearest mapped ancestor.\n- The Python, TypeScript, and CSS tests show unmapped statements and at-rules producing no nodes.\n\n**Markdown directive containers**\n- `paragraphs_and_nested_directives_have_independent_source_ranges` checks source ranges and containment.\n- `unfinished_directives_retain_their_body_and_leave_the_outer_closer_outside` and `nested_fence_lengths_and_closer_whitespace_preserve_the_right_containers` check nesting, fence lengths, and unclosed fences.\n- `literal_code_inline_code_and_html_shield_directive_looking_text` checks that no directive is recognized inside backtick or tilde fences, inline code, or raw HTML.\n\n**Attached siblings, hashes, and line ranges**\n- `hashes_skip_whitespace_and_plain_comments_but_not_doc_comments` and `identity_hashes_include_own_attached_siblings_but_not_descendants` check that attached doc comments and attributes count toward a node's line range and hash.\n- `line_queries_find_innermost_nodes` checks lookups by line.\n\n**Root node and no fallback kinds**\n- `file_level_inner_doc_comments_and_unmapped_code_belong_to_the_root` and the Python and Markdown front-matter assertions cover the root node and source that belongs to no other node.\n- `no_profile_invents_fallback_kinds` checks every profile for invented fallback kinds.\n\n**Comments are not nodes**\n- Comment lines appear in the CSS, TOML, YAML, Markdown, Python, and Rust sources and never in the outline nodes, in the tests above.\n\n**Documentation**\n- `every_profile_mapping_is_documented` checks the grammar-to-kind mapping and the naming column against `md/reference.md`.\n\n**Redaction**\n- `redaction_never_changes_an_outline` adds further coverage.\n\nI found no input class, boundary, or failure case the text names that lacks a test with a matching assertion.",
  "references": "080a9a830586c9ff8d259b3017c52823976f3482cd9c5bd837640a4002c8c676",
